-- title:
--   Maximality of chart primes over a maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ a nonzero element. Write $A =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra $R[j] =$ `Algebra.adjoin R {j}`, and let `jChartFin R F j` denote $j$ regarded as an element of $A$. Let $\mathfrak{m} \subseteq R$ be a maximal ideal, and let $y$ be a point of the scheme `XFin R F j` $= \operatorname{Spec} A$, so that $y$ corresponds to a prime ideal $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ of $A$. Assume: (i) the ideal of $A$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak{m}$ under the structure map $R \to A$ is contained in $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; and (ii) there is a polynomial $P \in R[X]$ whose reduction modulo $\mathfrak{m}$ is nonzero in $(R/\mathfrak{m})[X]$ and which satisfies $P(j) \in y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, the evaluation being taken at `jChartFin R F j` in $A$. Then the prime $y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ is a maximal ideal of $A$; and, in addition, if $A$ is an $R$-algebra of finite type, then the residue ring $A / y.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ is a finite $R$-module.
--
--   This is the standard criterion that a prime of an integral extension lying over a maximal ideal of the base, at which the adjoined coordinate becomes algebraic over the residue field, is a closed point with finite residue field extension; here it is stated for the $j$-finite chart ring of the two-chart integral model of $(F, j)$ over $R$, namely the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$. It is used in the analysis of points of the special fibres of integral models of the modular curves $X_1(p)$ and $X_1(p) \cap X_0(\,\cdot\,)$, where supersingular $j$-invariants are algebraic over the residue field and the corresponding chart points must be recognised as closed points with finite residue extension.
